# The whole assignment in one run: execute the requests top to bottom.
# Later requests take ids from earlier responses ({{name.response.body...}}, Visual Studio 17.12+).
# Every run creates new halls, so the scenario can be repeated on the same database.

@host = http://localhost:5112
@day = 2030-09-01

### 1. Add a hall with services (assignment 1)
# @name createHall
POST {{host}}/api/halls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Зал D",
  "capacity": 40,
  "pricePerHour": 1800,
  "services": [
    { "name": "Проєктор", "price": 500 },
    { "name": "Wi-Fi", "price": 300 }
  ]
}

### 2. The new hall with the ids of its services
# @name hall
GET {{host}}/api/halls/{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}

### 3. Change the price 1800 -> 2500 (assignment 2)
PUT {{host}}/api/halls/{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Зал D",
  "capacity": 40,
  "pricePerHour": 2500
}

### 4. Add the "Звук" service for 700 (assignment 2)
POST {{host}}/api/halls/{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Звук",
  "price": 700
}

### 5. Free halls for 40 people, 10:00-14:00 (assignment 4)
GET {{host}}/api/halls/available?start={{day}}T10:00:00&end={{day}}T14:00:00&minCapacity=40

### 6. Book the new hall 10:00-14:00 with Wi-Fi (assignment 5)
# Rent: 2 h x 2500 + 2 h x 2875 (peak +15%) = 10750, Wi-Fi 300, total 11050
# @name booking
POST {{host}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hallId": "{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T10:00:00",
  "duration": "04:00:00",
  "serviceIds": [ "{{hall.response.body.$.services[0].id}}" ]
}

### 7. The same hall at 11:00 -> 409, it is already booked
POST {{host}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hallId": "{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T11:00:00",
  "duration": "02:00:00",
  "serviceIds": []
}

### 8. The booking confirmation again
GET {{host}}/api/bookings/{{booking.response.body.$.id}}

### 9. Delete the hall -> 409, it has an upcoming booking (assignment 3)
DELETE {{host}}/api/halls/{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}

### 10. A hall without bookings
# @name spareHall
POST {{host}}/api/halls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Зал E",
  "capacity": 20,
  "pricePerHour": 1000,
  "services": []
}

### 11. ...can be deleted -> 204 (assignment 3)
DELETE {{host}}/api/halls/{{spareHall.response.body.$.id}}

### 12. ...and is gone -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/halls/{{spareHall.response.body.$.id}}

### 13. Validation -> 400 with every error at once
POST {{host}}/api/halls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "capacity": 0,
  "pricePerHour": -5,
  "services": [ { "name": "Проєктор", "price": 0 } ]
}

### 14. Outside working hours (06:00-23:00) -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "hallId": "{{createHall.response.body.$.id}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T22:00:00",
  "duration": "02:00:00",
  "serviceIds": []
}

### 15. Report: halls for September 2030 (bookings from step 6 included)
# Hall D: 4 h out of 17 h x 30 days = 0.78% occupancy, revenue 11050
GET {{host}}/api/reports/halls?from=2030-09-01&to=2030-10-01

### 16. Report: services for September 2030
GET {{host}}/api/reports/services?from=2030-09-01&to=2030-10-01

### 17. Report with a wrong period -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/reports/halls?from=2030-10-01&to=2030-09-01
